e="color:transparent" src="/nextjs/images/ProductSolutions/info.svg"/><div class="style-module-scss-module__h0M7Qq__riskotooltiptext style-module-scss-module__h0M7Qq__benchwidth style-module-scss-module__h0M7Qq__entryposition"><div class="style-module-scss-module__h0M7Qq__tooltipcolor"><div class="drupal"><p>An entry load is a fee charged to investors when they purchase units of a Mutual Fund scheme. This fee was used to cover distribution and marketing expenses incurred by the Asset Management Company (AMC). Currently, Mutual Funds in India do not levy entry loads.</p>
